## How to Use

### 1. Set Up Locally

```bash
# Clone or download these files to a directory
mkdir tafel-app-v1
cd tafel-app-v1

# Copy index.html and tlogic.js into this directory

# Start a local HTTP server (required for OIDC redirect to work)
python3 -m http.server 8000
# or: npx http-server
# or: node -m http-server

# Open browser: http://localhost:8000
```

### 2. Test Login

1. Click **"🔐 Log In with Solid"**
2. Enter your Pod provider URL:
   - `https://solidweb.org` (public provider)
   - `https://pod.inrupt.com` (Inrupt Pod Space)
   - `https://herford.meisdata.io` (your own server)
3. You'll be redirected to OIDC login
4. After login, you'll see 7 profile parameters

### 3. Interpret the Parameters

| # | Parameter | Meaning | Use Case |
|---|-----------|---------|----------|
| 1 | **WebID** | Your unique Solid identifier | Reference for ACL, ownership |
| 2 | **Display Name** | Your vCard:fn or foaf:name | UI greeting ("Hello, {name}!") |
| 3 | **Preferences** | Link to your preferences file | Reserved for future settings |
| 4 | **Public Type Index** | Path to your public type registry | Discover public data |
| 5 | **Private Type Index** | Path to your private type registry | Discover private data |
| 6 | **Storage Root** | Your Pod's root directory | Base path for all data |
| 7 | **OIDC Issuer** | Your Pod provider | Which server authenticates you |

**In iteration 2**, these will be used to:
- Locate the Org Pod (`herford.meisdata.io` or `bielefeld.meisdata.io`)
- Fetch appointments and locations
- Detect user role (consumer vs. staff)
- Store/retrieve personal data

